DEMO_DOCUMENT = [
    "Agentic AI refers to systems that can perceive goals, reason over available information, plan actions, use tools, and adapt based on feedback. Unlike a single-turn language model, an agentic system can coordinate multiple steps toward an objective.",
    "Traditional automation follows predefined rules and predictable paths. Agentic systems are more flexible: they can select tools, break a goal into sub-tasks, make decisions under uncertainty, and revise a plan when observations change.",
    "Core components of an agentic architecture include a reasoning model, planning and task decomposition, tools or actions, memory, an environment or observation loop, and orchestration that controls state transitions between steps.",
    "Memory lets an agent retain useful information across steps or conversations. Short-term working memory supports the current task, while long-term memory can store durable facts, prior interactions, preferences, or learned procedures.",
    "A grounded RAG assistant should retrieve relevant document passages before generating an answer. It should use only those passages, cite or expose the supporting context, and explicitly refuse when the source does not contain enough information.",
]
